    <h1>Privacy Policy for ScamJacket</h1>
    <div class="meta">
        <strong>Effective Date:</strong> April 20, 2026<br>
        <strong>Developer:</strong> Pankaj Sejwal (SymbolArc Systems)<br>
        <strong>Package:</strong> <code>com.sejwal.ScamJacket</code>
    </div>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>ScamJacket</strong>, provided by 
        <strong>SymbolArc Systems</strong>, accesses, uses, stores, and protects data on your device. 
        ScamJacket is a device-side security and app protection tool.
    </p>

    <div class="box">
        <strong>The Short Version:</strong> ScamJacket operates entirely on your device. Your messages, OTPs, security data, and app usage information never leave your phone. There are no servers, no accounts, no analytics, and no third-party SDKs of any kind.
    </div>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Local Operation:</strong> ScamJacket is designed to work primarily on your device.</li>
        <li><strong>No Backend:</strong> We do not operate an app backend; we cannot see your data.</li>
        <li><strong>Zero Data Sale:</strong> We do not sell your data or use advertising SDKs.</li>
        <li><strong>No Tracking:</strong> We do not use analytics or crash reporting SDKs.</li>
        <li><strong>No Cloud Sync:</strong> <code>android:allowBackup</code> is explicitly disabled to prevent data from leaving your device via OS backups.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data the App Accesses or Handles</h2>

    <h3>1. App usage and foreground information</h3>
    <p>Uses <code>UsageStatsManager</code> to detect the active app to apply app locking and scheduled blocking.</p>

    <h3>2. Installed app inventory</h3>
    <p>Queries <code>QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES</code> to allow you to select apps to block, identify finance apps for protection, and scan for malicious remote access tools.</p>

    <h3>3. SMS and MMS data</h3>
    <p>When set as the default SMS app, ScamJacket processes messages to support the <strong>OTP Vault</strong> and messaging features. OTPs are extracted and stored in a hardware-encrypted vault locally.</p>

    <h3>4. Notification access</h3>
    <p>Detects notification-listener changes to alert you if a suspicious app is trying to read your notifications.</p>

    <h3>5. Phone state (READ_PHONE_STATE)</h3>
    <p>Detects call-forwarding indicators to warn you about potential scam-related device compromises.</p>

    <h3>6. VPN / Network Blocking</h3>
    <p>Uses <code>VpnService</code> to create a local "dead-end" tunnel. This blocks internet access for selected finance apps during risk conditions. <strong>No traffic is read, logged, or transmitted.</strong></p>

    <h3>7. Biometric & PIN Authentication</h3>
    <p>Uses Android <code>BiometricPrompt</code> and Salted Hashes for PINs. We do not receive or store your actual biometric templates; authentication is handled by the OS.</p>

    <h2>Data Storage & Security</h2>
    <p>
        All sensitive data (like the OTP Vault) is encrypted using <strong>AES-256-GCM</strong>. Encryption keys are stored in the <strong>Android Keystore</strong>, which is hardware-backed on supported devices. This means keys cannot be extracted from the device.
    </p>

    <h2>User Choice and Control</h2>
    <p>You remain in full control of your data. You can:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Revoke any permission in Android Settings at any time.</li>
        <li>Clear the OTP Vault or Security Alerts within the app.</li>
        <li><strong>Uninstall the app:</strong> This immediately and permanently deletes all data stored by ScamJacket from your device.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>ScamJacket does not knowingly collect any data from anyone, including children. Since no data leaves the device, it is inherently compliant with COPPA and similar regulations.</p>

